  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Ideogram pricing: the credit system explained</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Ideogram uses a credit-based pricing model that is simple but requires careful arithmetic for cost estimation. Credits are purchased in bundles: $10 gives 1,000 credits, $50 gives 5,500 credits (10% bonus), $100 gives 12,000 credits (20% bonus), and $500 gives 65,000 credits (30% bonus). Each standard generation costs 4 credits per image, and each prompt returns 4 images by default (16 credits total). A Turbo generation costs 8 credits per image (32 credits per 4-image batch). Canvas editing costs 2-6 credits per operation depending on the type (erase-and-fill 2 credits, inpainting 4 credits, outpainting 6 credits). Describe costs 1 credit per image.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">For a content team producing 500 social media images per month (each requiring text-heavy generation with 1-2 regenerations on average), the monthly cost is roughly $40-80 on the standard tier. For an e-commerce team generating 5,000 product mockups per month, the cost is $400-800. At the $100 credit bundle (12,000 credits), each standard image-generation batch (4 images) costs about $0.13 in credits, or $0.033 per individual image — comparable to DALL-E 3's $0.04 per image generation and significantly cheaper than Midjourney's per-minute GPU billing for batch workloads.</p>

