        <td class="px-4 py-2">$8-16</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-t">
        <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Enterprise batch processing</td>
        <td class="px-4 py-2">100,000+ images</td>
        <td class="px-4 py-2">800K+ credits</td>
        <td class="px-4 py-2">$4,000+ ($500 bundle rate)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Ideogram vs Midjourney vs DALL-E 3 vs Stable Diffusion 3.5</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">The image generation API market in 2026 has four credible contenders, and the right choice depends entirely on the workload. Midjourney V8 leads on subjective image quality (MOS 4.51, the highest in the market) but has no native text rendering and a Discord-only API that requires webhook-based polling. DALL-E 3 is the best integration with the OpenAI ecosystem and has good text rendering (82% accuracy) but costs $0.04 per image and has the strictest content policy. Stable Diffusion 3.5 is open-weight (self-hostable) and the cheapest at $0.0065 per image via the Stability AI API, but has the lowest text accuracy (71%) and inconsistent quality across diverse prompts.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Ideogram 3.0 occupies the sweet spot for any use case where the image contains visible text: social media graphics, product mockups, movie posters, infographics, educational diagrams, and presentation slides. For pure aesthetic generation (landscapes, abstract art, concept art), Midjourney V8 is still the consensus choice. For use cases that require both text and aesthetics — think a cinematic movie poster with a title treatment — Ideogram 3.0's ability to merge readable text with high-quality visuals in a single API call is a genuinely unique capability in the 2026 market.</p>

