  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Magic Prompt: the auto-prompt-engineer feature</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Ideogram's Magic Prompt is an optional feature that automatically rewrites the user's input prompt before passing it to the generation model. According to Ideogram's internal testing, Magic Prompt improves generation success rate (first-pass acceptance) by 23 percentage points across all prompt categories. For a prompt like <em>"a coffee shop menu board with today's specials in chalk font"</em>, Magic Prompt expands it to an optimized version that specifies typography details, lighting, depth of field, and text positioning — effectively doing the prompt engineering work that a human would otherwise need 5-10 iterations to discover.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Magic Prompt is enabled by default and can be disabled by setting the <code>magic_prompt</code> parameter to <code>false</code> in the generation request. For advanced users who have a specific vision and want pixel-level control, disabling Magic Prompt and writing raw prompts gives more predictability. For most users, keeping Magic Prompt on produces better images with less iteration, which is the more economically efficient choice given the per-generation credit cost.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Ideogram Canvas: inpainting, outpainting, and style transfer</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Ideogram Canvas is the editing suite exposed through the <code>/edit</code> and <code>/canvas</code> endpoints. Inpainting accepts a base image and a mask (a PNG with white pixels where the AI should generate, black pixels where it should preserve), along with a prompt describing the replacement content. The inpainting quality is high enough that it can replace the traditional Photoshop workflow for most content-generation tasks: changing a product's background, replacing a logo on a storefront, or adding a character to an existing scene.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Outpainting extends the canvas in any direction (up, down, left, right) with AI-generated content that matches the original style. For an e-commerce team creating hero images for product detail pages, outpainting is the most efficient path: generate a tight product shot, then outpaint to fill the hero banner dimensions with a compatible environment. Style transfer applies the aesthetic of a reference image to a new generation, which is useful for maintaining brand consistency across a campaign.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">All Canvas operations preserve Ideogram's text rendering quality, which means you can generate a social media card with text, then inpaint to fix a typo without re-generating the entire image. This is a genuinely useful workflow that no competitor offers in a single API call: generate once, edit the text region, ship.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">The Describe endpoint: reverse-engineering prompts from images</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Ideogram Describe accepts an image and returns a text prompt that would approximately reproduce it. The endpoint is useful for three workflows: (1) building a prompt library from a collection of reference images, (2) understanding the prompt that generated a particular output from a known seed, and (3) discovering the Magic Prompt expansion for a raw prompt. Describe runs at 1 credit per image (roughly $0.01 at the $100 bundle rate) and returns a single prompt string with no configuration options.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">The quality of Describe's output is comparable to GPT-4o's image analysis at roughly 10% of the cost (1 credit vs the LLM API cost of processing an image input). For a team building a prompt-engineering pipeline, the combination of Describe + Magic Prompt creates a useful feedback loop: Describe the output, feed the prompt back through Magic Prompt, generate a new version, and iterate.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Ideogram in production: rate limits, moderation, and API quirks</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">The default API tier allows 60 requests per minute and 10,000 images per day. The Scale tier ($500/month commit, available through a support ticket) lifts this to 300 RPM and 100,000 images/day. For enterprise customers, Ideogram offers custom rate limits starting at $5,000/month with dedicated GPU capacity and SLA guarantees. All tiers include built-in content moderation: Ideogram applies both automated NSFW filtering and a prompt-level text filter for restricted terms.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">The most important API quirk for developers is that all requests are synchronous HTTPS POSTs with no streaming support. Generation time averages 3-8 seconds for standard tier and 1.5-3 seconds for Turbo tier, and the connection must remain open during generation. For high-throughput batch processing, the correct pattern is to parallelize requests across multiple API keys or apply for Scale tier rate limits. There is no webhook callback mode — the response body contains the generated images as base64-encoded data URIs or as URLs to temporary S3-hosted files (expiring in 24 hours).</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Another operational consideration is that Ideogram does not support transparent PNG output. All images are returned as JPG or WebP, which means compositing Ideogram-generated images into an existing design requires a background-removal step. For a text-over-photo workflow (the most common use case), this is not an issue because the text is part of the rasterized image. For a compositing workflow where Ideogram generates only the visual element and the developer adds text separately, the lack of alpha channel output is a meaningful limitation.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Can I self-host Ideogram?</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">No — Ideogram 3.0 is not open-weight and is API-only, the same posture as Midjourney and DALL-E 3. The model weights have never been published, and Ideogram has not indicated any plans for self-hosted deployment. For teams that require self-hosted image generation (regulated industries, air-gapped environments, ultra-high-volume workloads exceeding 500K images/month), the credible open-weight alternatives are Stable Diffusion 3.5 (Stability AI, Apache 2.0, best quality among open models with 71% text accuracy) and FLUX.2 Pro (Black Forest Labs, API with a non-commercial open-weight option, 74% text accuracy). Neither matches Ideogram for text rendering, but both are self-hostable and can be integrated into a two-stage pipeline: generate the base image in SD3.5/FLUX, add text overlay in a separate compositing step.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">What about the Ideogram affiliate program?</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Ideogram does not have a public affiliate or referral program as of July 2026. There is no affiliate dashboard, referral link generator, or disclosed commission structure. For content sites that want to monetize Ideogram coverage, the recommended pattern is to link to the platform as a tool recommendation and use FreeModel for related LLM API spend (since an image+text generation workflow often pairs with an LLM for prompt generation and copywriting). Contact partnerships@ideogram.ai for custom partnership arrangements for high-volume content sites.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Final verdict: is Ideogram worth it in 2026?</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Yes — for any workload where the generated image contains visible text, Ideogram 3.0 is the best API in the market by a significant margin. The 94% character-level accuracy on English text is the difference between a self-serve automated workflow and a human-in-the-loop editing pipeline. At $0.033-$0.067 per image at the optimal credit bundle pricing, Ideogram is cost-competitive with DALL-E 3 and significantly cheaper than a two-stage Midjourney+Photoshop pipeline. The Magic Prompt feature reduces iteration time, and the Canvas editing suite (inpainting, outpainting, style transfer) makes the API useful beyond batch generation.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">If your use case is pure aesthetic image generation (landscapes, abstract art, fashion concepts) with no text requirement, Midjourney V8 is still the right API. If your use case requires open-weight self-hosting or the lowest possible per-image cost, Stable Diffusion 3.5 or FLUX.2 Pro are better choices. For everything in between — social media content, e-commerce mockups, infographics, educational diagrams, marketing materials — Ideogram 3.0 is the default image generation API in 2026.</p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">FAQ</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: How much does the Ideogram API cost?</strong><br>A: Credit-based pricing: $1 = 100 credits. Standard generation 4 credits/image (4 images per prompt = 16 credits). Turbo 8 credits/image. Canvas editing 2-6 credits. Describe 1 credit. At the $100 bundle (12,000 credits), each standard image costs about $0.033.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: Is there a free tier for the Ideogram API?</strong><br>A: Yes — $1 in free credits (100 credits) on signup, enough for approximately 25 standard image generations. After that, prepaid credit bundles are required ($10 minimum). No ongoing free tier.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: How good is Ideogram's text rendering?</strong><br>A: 94.2% character-level accuracy on English benchmarks, the highest among commercial image APIs. Compares to DALL-E 3 (82%), Midjourney V8 (78%), Stable Diffusion 3.5 (71%). CJK accuracy is 87% vs 52-68% for competitors.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: Can I use Ideogram from inside China?</strong><br>A: Access requires a proxy (AWS us-east-1/us-west-2 hosts). China-issued credit cards are not accepted for payment as of July 2026. Consider Aliyun Bailian Tongyi Wanxiang for a China-direct alternative.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: How does Ideogram compare to Midjourney?</strong><br>A: Midjourney V8 has higher aesthetic quality (MOS 4.51 vs Ideogram's 4.38) but no text rendering capability. Ideogram uses REST API; Midjourney uses Discord-only. For text-centric use cases, Ideogram is the better choice.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: Does Ideogram support image editing?</strong><br>A: Yes — Ideogram Canvas supports inpainting, outpainting, style transfer, and erase-and-fill. Costs 2-6 credits per edit. All edits preserve text rendering quality.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: Does Ideogram have an affiliate program?</strong><br>A: Not currently. For affiliate revenue from related AI image tools, use FreeModel (an aggregator with a public affiliate program) for the LLM prompt-generation side of the workflow.</p>

  <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Q: What is the Ideogram API rate limit?</strong><br>A: Default: 60 RPM, 10,000 images/day. Scale tier ($500/month commit): 300 RPM, 100K images/day. Enterprise: custom SLAs from $5,000/month.</p>

